// PARAM: --analysis interval
// A PROVED verdict makes no reachability claim. x = 4 * n at u32 is a multiple
// of 4 modulo 2^32, since 4 divides 2^32, so it is never 1, 2 or 3 and no run
// reaches the check. The interval analysis cannot see that and keeps x = [1,3]
// there, where x > 0 holds. The verdict is PROVED, and it is sound: it says
// that x > 0 holds whenever a run reaches the check, which is vacuous.
// Backs the example in thesis section 10.5.
fun main() {
  u32 n;
  u32 x = 4 * n;
  if (0 < x && x < 4) {
    __voblint_check(x > 0);  // PROVED
  }
}
